          "ans": "0.4",
          "why": "−0.4 is 0.4 units from 0. So |−0.4| = 0.4.",
          "clue": "How far is −0.4 from 0 on the number line?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "step": "method",
          "text": "Absolute values of some real numbers.",
          "steps": [
            "|4| = 4.",
            "|−2| = 2, because −2 is 2 units from 0.",
            "|1/2| = 1/2 and |−0.4| = 0.4.",
            "|−√2| = √2.",
            "|2 − √8| = √8 − 2, because 2 − √8 < 0."
          ],
          "ref": "Example 1"
        },
        {
          "kind": "mcq",
          "step": "practise",
          "graded": true,
          "title": "Careful with roots",
          "text": "What is |3 − √10|?",
          "opts": [
            "3 − √10",
            "√10 − 3",
            "3 + √10",
            "−3 − √10"
          ],
          "ans": "√10 − 3",
          "why": "√10 ≈ 3.16 > 3, so 3 − √10 is negative and its absolute value is √10 − 3.",
          "clue": "Is 3 − √10 positive or negative?",
          "worked": "√10 ≈ 3.16, so 3 − √10 ≈ −0.16 < 0. For a negative x, |x| = −x. So |3 − √10| = −(3 − √10) = √10 − 3."
        },
        {
          "kind": "read",
          "step": "read",
          "title": "Distance between two numbers",
          "paras": [
            "Example 2: The distance between −3 and 4 is 7 units.",
            "|a − b| = |−3 − 4| = |−7| = 7, and |b − a| = |4 − (−3)| = 7.",
            "The distance between a and b is |a − b|, and |a − b| = |b − a|."
          ],
          "note": "Figure 1.8: drag a and b on the number line; the distance |a − b| never goes negative."
        },
        {
          "kind": "name",
          "step": "name",
          "title": "Distance on the line",
          "defs": [
            [
              "Distance between a and b",
              "|a − b|. The order does not matter: |a − b| = |b − a|."
            ]
          ]
